1. MVP BOUNDARY AND IMPLEMENTATION STRATEGY
==================================================

Build a complete, interactive product prototype with the major screens and workflows available for stakeholder review.

This first phase uses synthetic data exclusively.

The objective is to demonstrate functional behavior and validate the product with accountants and financial advisors before production implementation.

Distinguish between:

A. Functional prototype workflows:
Real UI interaction with consistent synthetic application state.

B. Simulated integrations:
Clearly labeled demonstrations of workflows requiring external services.

C. Production integrations:
Explicitly excluded from this first phase unless already available and authorized.

Never simulate a successful government filing, bank connection, WhatsApp transmission, or legally compliant tax submission.

All prototype-generated tax documents must clearly display:
"BORRADOR DE DEMOSTRACIÓN — SIN VALIDEZ TRIBUTARIA".

All prototype-generated invoices must clearly display:
"DOCUMENTO DE DEMOSTRACIÓN — NO VÁLIDO PARA FACTURACIÓN REAL".

Create a centralized demo data service and persistence abstraction.

Avoid scattered hardcoded data in individual components.

All screens must reflect the same underlying synthetic records.

For example, changing an invoice classification must update the relevant accounting records, reporting views, and tax projections within the prototype.

Do not create a fake backend simply to imitate an API.

Use a clearly separated prototype data adapter first.

Prepare, but do not prematurely implement, the production adapter for the PHP/MySQL API.

Do not create cloud infrastructure, databases, secrets, or external accounts during this phase.

